      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Sum the first five prime numbers.\n3. Divide the sum by the sixth prime number.\n4. Find the remainder of the division.\n\n**Step 1: Identify the first six prime numbers.**\n\nThe first six prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13 \\]\n\n**Step 2: Sum the first five prime numbers.**\n\nThe first five prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 \\]\n\nWe sum these numbers:\n\\[ 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 \\]\n\nLet's add them step-by-step:\n\\[ 2 + 3 = 5 \\]\n\\[ 5 + 5 = 10 \\]\n\\[ 10 + 7 = 17 \\]\n\\[ 17 + 11 = 28 \\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five prime numbers is:\n\\[ 28 \\]\n\n**Step 3: Divide the sum by the sixth prime number.**\n\nThe sixth prime number is:\n\\[ 13 \\]\n\nWe need to divide 28 by 13:\n\\[ 28 \\div 13 \\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\\[ 28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nThis means:\n\\[ 28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2 \\]\n\nThe quotient is 2, and the remainder is 2.\n\n**Step 4: Find the remainder of the division.**\n\nThe remainder when 28 is divided by 13 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2} \\]",
